            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-61731-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-61731 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Building a malicious file with cmd/go can cause can cause a write to an attacker-controlled file with partial control of the file content. The \"#cgo pkg-config:\" directive in a Go source file provides command-line arguments to provide to the Go pkg-config command. An attacker can provide a \"--log-file\" argument to this directive, causing pkg-config to write to an attacker-controlled location."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-61731\nSeverity: high\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.19.7\nFix Version: 1.24.12,1.25.6\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/bin/kube-controllers\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-61731](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-61731)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-61731**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | stdlib  | go1.19.7  | 1.24.12,1.25.6  | go-module  | /usr/bin/kube-controllers  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-61731](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-61731)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.19.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-29403-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-29403 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "On Unix platforms, the Go runtime does not behave differently when a binary is run with the setuid/setgid bits. This can be dangerous in certain cases, such as when dumping memory state, or assuming the status of standard i/o file descriptors. If a setuid/setgid binary is executed with standard I/O file descriptors closed, opening any files can result in unexpected content being read or written with elevated privileges. Similarly, if a setuid/setgid program is terminated, either via panic or signal, it may leak the contents of its registers."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-29403\nSeverity: high\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.19.7\nFix Version: 1.19.10,1.20.5\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/bin/check-status\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-29403](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-29403)",
